      "expect": "reject",
      "reason": "The application id must match ^[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$ — one hostname label, at most 63 characters: an uppercase letter is not a label character, and an id that could not be a label would name an application no host could carry."
    },
    {
      "name": "apps-reject-id-not-a-host-label",
      "kind": "apps",
      "payload": {
        "ok": true,
        "computer_connected": true,
        "code": "ready",
        "apps": [
          {
            "id": "my_app",
            "name": "Jellyfin",
            "description": "媒体库",
            "icon": "🎬",
            "accent": "#2563eb",
            "launch_fragment": "#/home",
            "computer_connected": true,
            "enabled": true,
            "running": true,
            "code": "ready"
          },
          {
            "id": "my.app",
            "name": "Jellyfin",
            "description": "媒体库",
            "icon": "🎬",
            "accent": "#2563eb",
            "launch_fragment": "#/home",
            "computer_connected": true,
            "enabled": true,
            "running": true,
            "code": "ready"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": "reject",
      "reason": "A public gateway serves an application at a host built under its own domain and the id is that host’s first label; a dot or an underscore cannot appear in a hostname label, so an id carrying one names an application no host could carry. The loose rule that tolerated them is gone — the server never speaks such an id."
    },
